ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: retention.seq.purge
display_id: SEQ-RETENTION-PURGE
module: retention
title: Purge a memory
summary: Decides what a purge covers and who may make it, then deletes every copy of that content and queues the cloud deletion.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: The owner or agent purges a memory, or the sweep purges a memory past its recovery window
operation: retention.op.purge
participants:
  - id: caller
    is: [actor.owner, actor.agent, retention.seq.sweep]
    label: Owner, agent or retention sweep
  - sys.daemon
  - id: db
    is: [sys.home]
    label: Stack database
items: []
parts:
  - retention.seq.purge.a
  - retention.seq.purge.b
rationale: >-
  The owner sees the cascade before anything is deleted, because a purge is
  irreversible and the evidence behind a memory may be what the owner actually
  wants gone. An agent's purge is the minimum that honors the request: one
  memory, no cascade, and never something the owner wrote or protected, since
  instructions injected into an agent could otherwise erase the memories that
  guard against them.
